{"data":[{"id":"10.48550/arxiv.2606.19350","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2606.19350","identifiers":[{"identifier":"2606.19350","identifierType":"arXiv"}],"creators":[{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Amogh","familyName":"Sheth","name":"Sheth, Amogh","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Andrew","familyName":"Lin","name":"Lin, Andrew","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Biruk","familyName":"Assefa","name":"Assefa, Biruk","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yi Wen","familyName":"Huang","name":"Huang, Yi Wen","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]},{"nameType":"Personal","givenName":"Yuhao","familyName":"Ge","name":"Ge, Yuhao","affiliation":[],"nameIdentifiers":[]}],"titles":[{"title":"Pruning via Causal Attribution Preserves Reasoning Performance in Large Language Models"}],"publisher":"arXiv","container":{},"publicationYear":2026,"subjects":[{"subject":"Computation and Language (cs.CL)","lang":"en","subjectScheme":"arXiv"},{"subject":"FOS: Computer and information sciences","subjectScheme":"Fields of Science and Technology (FOS)"}],"contributors":[],"dates":[{"date":"2026-04-27T01:44:10Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-06-19T00:00:18Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v1"},{"date":"2026-10-27T05:55:55Z","dateType":"Submitted","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-10-28T00:43:38Z","dateType":"Updated","dateInformation":"v2"},{"date":"2026-06","dateType":"Available","dateInformation":"v1"}],"language":null,"types":{"schemaOrg":"CreativeWork","resourceTypeGeneral":"Preprint","citeproc":"article","bibtex":"misc","ris":"GEN","resourceType":"Article"},"relatedIdentifiers":[],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":[],"formats":[],"version":"2","rightsList":[{"rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX","rightsUri":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode","schemeUri":"https://spdx.org/licenses/","rights":"Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International","rightsIdentifier":"cc-by-4.0"}],"descriptions":[{"descriptionType":"Abstract","description":"Large language models (LLMs) excel at multi-step reasoning but incur substantial inference cost. We introduce Causal Attribution Pruning (CAP), a training-free method that identifies critical attention heads by measuring their causal impact on reasoning tasks and uses these head-level scores to guide fine-grained weight pruning. For each attention head, CAP estimates the expected performance degradation when the head is masked during forward passes on a small calibration set of reasoning problems. These causal scores are then converted into weight-level importance values for the corresponding projection matrices. Unlike magnitude-only or activation-based criteria, CAP's interventional measurement directly captures each head's functional contribution, yielding relative accuracy gains of up to 61% over Wanda on ARC-Challenge at 20% sparsity. We evaluate CAP on GSM8K, StrategyQA, and ARC-Challenge using Llama-3-8B-Instruct and Mistral-7B-Instruct at 10%, 20%, and 50% sparsity. At moderate sparsity (10-20%), CAP improves over Wanda in most model-benchmark configurations. with especially large gains on ARC-Challenge for Llama-3. Our results suggest that attention-head-level causal attribution can better preserve reasoning performance on downstream benchmarks than correlational pruning criteria at equivalent sparsity, while remaining limited by coarse MLP attribution at 50% sparsity."},{"descriptionType":"Other","description":"Accepted at the ICLR 2026 Workshop on LLM Reasoning. 13 pages, 2 figures"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.19350","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":1,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"mds","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"downloadCount":0,"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":0,"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":0,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2026-06-19T01:47:20Z","registered":"2026-06-19T01:47:21Z","published":null,"updated":"2026-10-28T03:19:24Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"arxiv.content","type":"clients"}}}}],"meta":{"total":222,"totalPages":222,"page":1},"links":{"self":"https://api.datacite.org/dois?client-id=arxiv.content\u0026query=registered%3a%5b2026-06-18T16%3a00%3a00Z+TO+2026-06-19T15%3a59%3a59Z%5d+AND+%28titles.title%3a%28%22language+model%22+OR+%22language+models%22+OR+LLM+OR+LLMs+OR+Transformer+OR+Transformers+OR+%22foundation+model%22+OR+%22foundation+models%22%29+OR+descriptions.description%3a%28%22language+model%22+OR+%22language+models%22+OR+LLM+OR+LLMs+OR+Transformer+OR+Transformers%29%29\u0026page[size]=1","next":"https://api.datacite.org/dois?client-id=arxiv.content\u0026page%5Bnumber%5D=2\u0026page%5Bsize%5D=1\u0026query=registered%3A%5B2026-06-18T16%3A00%3A00Z+TO+2026-06-19T15%3A59%3A59Z%5D+AND+%28titles.title%3A%28%22language+model%22+OR+%22language+models%22+OR+LLM+OR+LLMs+OR+Transformer+OR+Transformers+OR+%22foundation+model%22+OR+%22foundation+models%22%29+OR+descriptions.description%3A%28%22language+model%22+OR+%22language+models%22+OR+LLM+OR+LLMs+OR+Transformer+OR+Transformers%29%29"}}